{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And I will make them hear My words, etc., that they may fear Me all the days.</b> It may be explained along the way of our Sages of blessed memory (Shabbat 146a) — Israel who stood at Mount Sinai, their pollution (זוֹהֲמָה) departed; and I explained in parashat Yitro that the cessation of their pollution was through the power of the mighty words of Elohim, so that their souls departed, and this constitutes the removal of pollution from them. And this is the meaning of <b>וְאַשְׁמִיעֵם אֶת דְּבָרָי</b> — namely, the Ten Commandments that came in might, as it is written (Exodus 20:1): ״וַיְדַבֵּר אֱלֹהִים אֵת כָּל הַדְּבָרִים״. And the reason I did this — <b>that they may fear Me all the days</b> — is through the removal of pollution from them, for it is that which prevents a person from fearing HaShem. And this is the reason Israel did not rebel against their honor and endured many troubles for many days beyond number, standing guard over the fear of HaShem — because their pollution departed, and the nature of their soul is to fear HaShem; for anyone in whom pollution does not separate between him and HaShem, it is his nature to fear HaShem, may He be exalted and blessed."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:06.537703779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}